IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa24-officers.l4: Part 36, "Liability of officer in default": ss 1121, 1122 and 1123 of the Companies Act 2006
-- (lines 16059-16084 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE ANSWERS FOR THE OTHER PARTS. Every offence section of the Act that says "an offence is committed
-- by ... every officer of the company who is in default" relies on s 1121. The seam name the plan gives is
-- `s 1121 the officer is in default`; the function that answers it is `s 1121 the person is an officer in default`
-- (both limbs: s 1121(2) "officer" and s 1121(3) "in default"), with the two limbs separately as
-- `s 1121(2) the person is an officer of the company` and `s 1121(3) the officer is in default`.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). Every decision function answers
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: the text says yes. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words ("means", "if",
-- "unless", a flat negative); each such branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`.
-- NOTHING: the text does not decide (lists without closing the list, "includes", silent, points outside the text,
-- limited by its own wording); each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`. A caller must never turn
-- NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Part 36: liability of officer in default (ss 1121 to 1123)`

-- ---- s 1121 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16061 | (1) This section has effect for the purposes of any provision of the Companies Acts to the effect that, in the event of contravention of an enactment in relation to a company, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 1121(1) Liability of officer in default: when the section has effect (src:16061)
GIVEN `the provision is one of the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision says that, on contravention of an enactment in relation to a company, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1121(1) the section has effect for the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision is one of the Companies Acts` AND `the provision says that, on contravention of an enactment in relation to a company, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section has effect for the purposes of any provision of the Companies Acts to the effect that"

-- The positions s 1121(2) names. Whether a person IS a director (ss 250, 251), is a manager, or is to be treated as
-- an officer for the provision in question (a rule of that provision) is a fact the caller states.
DECLARE `s 1121(2) position of the person` IS ONE OF
    `s 1121(2)(a) a director`
    `s 1121(2)(a) a manager`
    `s 1121(2)(a) a secretary`
    `s 1121(2)(b) a person treated as an officer of the company for the purposes of the provision in question`
    `s 1121(2) none of these positions`

-- src:16062 | (2) For this purpose “officer” includes—
-- src:16063 | (a) any director, manager or secretary, and
-- src:16064 | (b) any person who is to be treated as an officer of the company for the purposes of the provision in question.
@ref s 1121(2) "officer" includes (src:16062-16064)
GIVEN position IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1121(2) the person is an officer of the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER position
    WHEN `s 1121(2)(a) a director` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1121(2)(a) a manager` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1121(2)(a) a secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1121(2)(b) a person treated as an officer of the company for the purposes of the provision in question` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1121(2) none of these positions` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“officer” includes" lists what the term includes and does not close the list

-- s 1121(3): the three limbs are inputs, as the plan says.
-- src:16065 | (3) An officer is “in default” for the purposes of the provision if he authorises or permits, participates in, or fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the contravention.
@ref s 1121(3) "in default" (src:16065)
GIVEN `authorises or permits the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `participates in the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1121(3) the officer is in default` MEANS
    IF       `authorises or permits the contravention`
          OR `participates in the contravention`
          OR `fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An officer is “in default” for the purposes of the provision if he authorises or permits, participates in, or fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the contravention"

-- What an officer's conduct is, as a record: the three limbs of s 1121(3), one field each.
DECLARE `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer` HAS
    `s 1121(3) authorises or permits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1121(3) participates in` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1121(3) fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Both limbs together: the person is an officer (s 1121(2)) who is in default (s 1121(3)), which is the person every
-- "officer in default" offence names. Not in default means not caught, whatever the person's office.
-- src:16062 | (2) For this purpose “officer” includes—
-- src:16063 | (a) any director, manager or secretary, and
-- src:16064 | (b) any person who is to be treated as an officer of the company for the purposes of the provision in question.
-- src:16065 | (3) An officer is “in default” for the purposes of the provision if he authorises or permits, participates in, or fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the contravention.
@ref s 1121(2)-(3) the person is an officer of the company who is in default (src:16062-16065)
GIVEN position IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person`
      conduct IS A `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1121 the person is an officer in default` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1121(3) the officer is in default` (conduct's `s 1121(3) authorises or permits`) (conduct's `s 1121(3) participates in`) (conduct's `s 1121(3) fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent`)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An officer is “in default” for the purposes of the provision if he authorises or permits, participates in, or fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent, the contravention"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 1121(2) the person is an officer of the company` position
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the conduct limbs are plain facts and cannot be unknown

-- ---- s 1122 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16067 | (1) Where a company is an officer of another company, it does not commit an offence as an officer in default unless one of its officers is in default.
@ref s 1122(1) A company that is an officer of another company (src:16067)
GIVEN `the company is an officer of another company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the company's officers is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1122(1) the company commits an offence as an officer in default` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is an officer of another company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company is an officer of another company"
    ELSE IF `one of the company's officers is in default`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar lifts when "one of its officers is in default" but the text does not say the company then commits the offence
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it does not commit an offence as an officer in default unless one of its officers is in default"

-- src:16068 | (2) Where any such offence is committed by a company the officer in question also commits the offence and is liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 1122(2) The officer in question also commits the offence (src:16068)
GIVEN `an offence as an officer in default is committed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the officer in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1122(2) the officer in question also commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `an offence as an officer in default is committed by the company` AND `the person is the officer in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any such offence is committed by a company the officer in question also commits the offence"

DECLARE `s 1122(3) term` IS ONE OF
    `s 1122(3) officer`
    `s 1122(3) in default`

-- s 1122(3): "officer" and "in default" have the meanings given by section 1121. The answer is the section number.
-- src:16069 | (3) In this section “officer” and “in default” have the meanings given by section 1121.
@ref s 1122(3) "officer" and "in default" (src:16069)
GIVEN term IS A `s 1122(3) term`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1122(3) the section that gives the meaning of the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `s 1122(3) officer` THEN 1121
    WHEN `s 1122(3) in default` THEN 1121

-- ---- s 1123 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1123 kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `s 1123 a company`
    `s 1123 a body corporate other than a company`
    `s 1123 a partnership`
    `s 1123 an unincorporated body other than a partnership`

-- src:16071 | (1) Section 1121 (liability of officers in default) applies to a body other than a company as it applies to a company.
@ref s 1123(1) Section 1121 applies to a body other than a company (src:16071)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1123 kind of body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1123(1) section 1121 applies to the body` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1123 a company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1) speaks of "a body other than a company"
    WHEN `s 1123 a body corporate other than a company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1123 a partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1123 an unincorporated body other than a partnership` THEN JUST TRUE

-- What a person must be, in each kind of body, to be read as "a director of the company" in s 1121(2)(a) (limb (a) of
-- subsections (2), (3) and (4)), and as "a manager or secretary of the company" (limb (b) of each).
DECLARE `s 1123 role of the person in the body` IS ONE OF
    `s 1123 a member of the body`
    `s 1123 a corresponding officer of the body`
    `s 1123 a member of the partnership`
    `s 1123 a member of the governing body`
    `s 1123 a manager, secretary or similar officer`
    `s 1123 some other role`

-- src:16072 | (2) As it applies in relation to a body corporate other than a company—
-- src:16073 | (a) the reference to a director of the company shall be read as referring—
-- src:16074 | (i) where the body's affairs are managed by its members, to a member of the body,
-- src:16075 | (ii) in any other case, to any corresponding officer of the body, and
-- src:16076 | (b) the reference to a manager or secretary of the company shall be read as referring to any manager, secretary or similar officer of the body.
-- src:16077 | (3) As it applies in relation to a partnership—
-- src:16078 | (a) the reference to a director of the company shall be read as referring to a member of the partnership, and
-- src:16079 | (b) the reference to a manager or secretary of the company shall be read as referring to any manager, secretary or similar officer of the partnership.
-- src:16080 | (4) As it applies in relation to an unincorporated body other than a partnership—
-- src:16081 | (a) the reference to a director of the company shall be read as referring—
-- src:16082 | (i) where the body's affairs are managed by its members, to a member of the body,
-- src:16083 | (ii) in any other case, to a member of the governing body, and
-- src:16084 | (b) the reference to a manager or secretary of the company shall be read as referring to any manager, secretary or similar officer of the body.
@ref s 1123(2)-(4) How section 1121 reads for a body corporate, a partnership and an unincorporated body (src:16072-16084)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1123 kind of body`
      `the body's affairs are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      role IS A `s 1123 role of the person in the body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1123 the person is read as a director for the purposes of section 1121(2)(a)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1123 a company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 1123 speaks of bodies other than a company
    WHEN `s 1123 a body corporate other than a company` THEN
        IF `the body's affairs are managed by its members`
        THEN IF role EQUALS `s 1123 a member of the body`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(i) where the body's affairs are managed by its members, to a member of the body"
        ELSE IF role EQUALS `s 1123 a corresponding officer of the body`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(ii) in any other case, to any corresponding officer of the body"
    WHEN `s 1123 a partnership` THEN
        IF role EQUALS `s 1123 a member of the partnership`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) the reference to a director of the company shall be read as referring to a member of the partnership"
    WHEN `s 1123 an unincorporated body other than a partnership` THEN
        IF `the body's affairs are managed by its members`
        THEN IF role EQUALS `s 1123 a member of the body`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(i) where the body's affairs are managed by its members, to a member of the body"
        ELSE IF role EQUALS `s 1123 a member of the governing body`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(ii) in any other case, to a member of the governing body"

@ref s 1123(2)(b), (3)(b), (4)(b) Manager or secretary (src:16075-16076) (src:16079) (src:16084)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1123 kind of body`
      role IS A `s 1123 role of the person in the body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1123 the person is read as a manager or secretary for the purposes of section 1121(2)(a)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1123 a company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 1123 speaks of bodies other than a company
    OTHERWISE
        IF role EQUALS `s 1123 a manager, secretary or similar officer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the reference to a manager or secretary of the company shall be read as referring to any manager, secretary or similar officer of the body"
